# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-autocad-progid-registry-probe-fails — the ProgID probe read no registry, and refused a working AutoCAD
#+STATUS: DONE (alfe 2.2.87, 2026-09-25) -- Windows-runner confirmation pending
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-autocad-progid-registry-probe

* Observed

pjb, on the Windows runner, with alfe 2.2.84:

#+begin_example
$ alfe --debug --verbose -norc --cad autocad -l $probe
alfe[verbose]: cli: --cad "autocad" -> acad-2022 C:/Program Files/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2022/acad.exe
...
alfe: alfe AUTOCAD backend error (phase DETECT): AutoCAD 2022 was requested, but no COM server for it is registered.
  Tried:
    AutoCAD.Application.24.1: not-registered
  Not falling back to AutoCAD.Application: ...
#+end_example

and, on another run, the softer form of the same wrong conclusion:

#+begin_example
alfe[warn]: backend AUTOCAD: no COM registration for AutoCAD 2022; using AutoCAD.Application (set $AUTOCAD_PROGID to pin one)
#+end_example

=AutoCAD.Application.24.1= IS registered on that host: the diagnostic in
alfe-autocad-cad-selection-ignores-com-progid.issue activated AutoCAD
2022 through it, CLSID {AA46BA8A-9825-40FD-8493-0BA3C4D5CEB5}. The
feature that shipped in alfe 2.2.79 therefore refused a working
installation -- worse than the bug it fixed, because it stops the run.

* Cause -- two defects

** 1. The probe could not read the registry at all

=%reg-query= ran =reg.exe= with =:output :string= and the default
external format. reg.exe writes in the CONSOLE CODE PAGE, and the runner
is French: =reg query ... /ve= labels the value =(Par défaut)=, whose
=é= is not valid UTF-8. The decoder signalled, the surrounding
=ignore-errors= swallowed the error, and every query returned NIL.

A NIL answer meant "not registered". It also means "reg.exe is not on
PATH", "the query failed", "this is not Windows" -- and, here, "the
output could not be decoded". Those are opposite conclusions and they
shared one representation.

** 2. =--cad autocad= was read as naming a release

=--cad autocad= asks for the LATEST AutoCAD; the release is then alfe's
own discovery, not a user claim. START-ENGINE passed
=:explicit-p (and (cli-options-cad options) t)=, so any =--cad= at all
turned a fallback into a hard failure. Only =--cad autocad-2022= (or
=acad-2022=) names a release.

* Fix — alfe 2.2.87

- =%run-capturing-text= reads a console program's output with
  =:external-format :latin-1=, a total decoder: every byte becomes a
  character and nothing signals. The parsed part (REG_SZ, a CLSID, a
  path) is ASCII regardless of the code page.
- =reg= and =reg.exe= are both tried, and each query is logged at
  =--debug= with the size of the answer.
- =*registry-probe-usable-function*= answers whether the registry can be
  read at all, by querying a value that exists on every Windows
  (=HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion= =ProductName=).
  When it cannot, an explicitly requested release gets its own versioned
  ProgID UNVERIFIED, with a warning, rather than a refusal; only a
  registry that ANSWERS and lacks the release is a hard failure.
- =RELEASE-NAMED-BY-DENOTATION= decides explicitness: =autocad-2022= ->
  "2022", =autocad= -> NIL. START-ENGINE uses it, so =--cad autocad=
  falls back and =--cad autocad-2022= still refuses another release.

* Tests

All three defects are covered, and each was seen RED before its fix:

- =%run-capturing-text= against a program emitting a byte that is not
  valid UTF-8 (=printf 'a \351 REG_SZ b'=) -- the defect reproduced
  without Windows; with the old decoder the capture fails;
- an unreadable registry yields the versioned ProgID for an explicit
  release, and a hard error only for a release outside the table;
- a registry that answers and lacks the release still fails;
- =--cad autocad= starts through START-ENGINE on the generic ProgID with
  AutoCAD 2022 discovered and unregistered, while =--cad autocad-2022=
  on the same registry fails.

alfe SBCL and CCL: 1103 checks, 0 failures.

* Ground truth from the runner

=probe:com-registration:autocad:windows= (manual, no CAD tag, starts no
AutoCAD) runs =scripts/probe-autocad-com-registration.ps1=: the console
code page, the control value, the generic ProgID, every registered
=AutoCAD.Application*=, each candidate's CLSID and LocalServer32, and
alfe's own resolution under =--print-command= for both =--cad autocad=
and =--cad autocad-2022=.

Still to do on the machine: run that job, confirm the ProgID resolves to
=AutoCAD.Application.24.1= and that =-l probe.lsp= gets past bootstrap
(the open acceptance criterion inherited from
issues/closed/alfe-autocad-cad-selection-ignores-com-progid.issue).

* Lesson

A probe that cannot run must not answer the question it was asked. The
failure was not the accented byte; it was that "no answer" and "the
answer is no" were the same value.
